{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And every firstling of a donkey.</b> Specifically a donkey, and not the firstling of horses or camels. And the reason for this is what the rabbis of blessed memory expounded, that the Egyptians were likened to donkeys, as it is said (Ezekiel 23:20): ״אשר בשר חמורים בשרם״. And furthermore, there was not a single one of Israel who did not bring up ninety donkeys with them, laden with silver and gold; therefore the commandment came that we redeem the firstling of a donkey and not of other animals, because the plague of the firstborn was upon the firstborn of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:37.326803133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}